hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2789","###\n Narrated to us Yunus bin Abd al-A'la, who informed us that Ibn Wahb reported, stating that Malik informed him. [In another chain]: Narrated to us Al-Fadl bin Ya'qub, who narrated that Muhammad bin Ja'far narrated, who narrated that Malik bin Anas narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aisha (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever has the sacrificial animal (Hady) with him"
"2790","'Abdah ibn 'Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Muhammad — that is, ibn Bishr al-'Abdi — informed us: from Muhammad — who is ibn 'Umar — from Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, who said: ""We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Hajj in three categories: Some of us entered ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah together; some of us entered ihram for Hajj alone; and some of us entered ihram for 'Umrah alone. Whoever entered ihram for 'Umrah and Hajj, it is not lawful for him to exit ihram from anything that was made unlawful for him until he completes the rites of Hajj. And whoever entered ihram for 'Umrah alone, then circumambulated the House and walked between Safa and Marwah, has completed his 'Umrah until he undertakes a new Hajj."""
